BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Grab your ticket\nand head downtown for a day and night of what Longmont does best - live local music\, unique venues\, good vibes\, and community spirit! Presented by Flatirons Bank.\nWith 60 performances at 16 venues throughout Downtown Longmont\, you don’t want to miss out on this day of fun and live music Downtown! We're so excited to bring our 2025 headliner Erica Brown to the WWMS! Full performance lineup and schedule are available on our website. This year's lineup won't disappoint\, and you don't want to miss out!\nGet your tickets before they sell out!\nFind all the information at the\nWinter Walkabout webpage\nHuge THANK YOU to all of our fantastic sponsors who make this event possible:\nThe Longmont Downtown Development Authority\, Longmont Creative District\, SouthState Bank\, Audio Curations\, 105.5 The Colorado Sound\, and all of our venues. We couldn't do this without you!\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/winter-walkabout-music-showcase
DTEND:20260208T043000Z
LOCATION:Downtown Longmont
DTSTART:20260207T210000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 2026 Winter Walkabout Music Showcase
UID:d0b26d35-6e94-4d54-b789-465f1bd891dd@d0b2.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special Songwriters in the Round style concert to benefit Recovery Cafe Longmont!\nConnected by Music is proud to support Recovery Cafe Longmont with a special no-tickets music show.\nThis event will feature talented local singer-songwriters:\nMarilyn Walker\nKaren Horan\nRobby Layton\nRecovery Café Longmont is growing and expanding in their capability to support the community. With the purchase and renovation of 801 Main Street\, they will be able to provide more opportunities for community in a healing\, supportive space.\nPlease RSVP at https://www.connectedbymusic.org/event-details/2026-benefit-for-recovery-cafe-longmont\nTime: 4:00 PM -5:30 PM\nLocation: Longmont Central Presbyterian Church\, 402 Kimbark St\, Longmont\, CO 80501\,\nCost: No cost to attend\, donations to Connected by Music with all funds going to Recovery Cafe Longmont\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/benefit-concert-for-recovery-cafe-longmont
DTEND:20260222T003000Z
LOCATION:Central Longmont Presbyterian Church
DTSTART:20260221T230000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 Benefit Concert for Recovery Cafe Longmont
UID:ed692685-8e43-444a-9a98-e3b10df67df2@ed69.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Curious about what it takes to spin records like a pro? Join us for a hands-on “Try It” class where local Longmont DJ Antonette will introduce you to the art of vinyl DJing. Antonette will walk you through the basics—gear\, beat-matching\, mixing and how DJs shape the vibe of a room—while giving a live demonstration on the decks.\nBring one or two of your own dance records if you’d like\; we'll work them into a set so you can hear your favorite tunes in the mix!\nNo experience needed—just a love of music and a willingness to try something new.Come hang out\, learn something cool\, and discover the magic behind the turntables.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/try-it-series-dj-using-vinyl-with-dj-antonette
DTEND:20260110T230000Z
LOCATION:Butterscotch Studios
DTSTART:20260110T210000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Electronic] Try It Series: DJ using vinyl with DJ Antonette
UID:fad99ba0-2672-42ef-a243-f79b3c9fed62@fad9.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:This is an intimate live show in downtown Longmont\, Colorado presented by The Soundpost Sessions at The Times Collaborative featuring two songwriters and host Monica Marie LaBonte all on stage swapping songs and stories in-the-round. Music is from 7:30-9:30\, doors at 7:00. Join us for this very special ongoing musical series every other month!\n$18 Advance (reserved seating)\n$20 Day of Show\nThe Artists:\nBritt Devens https://www.brittdevens.com/\nBritt Devens is a musician who writes songs about hope\, heartbreak\, and recovery. A native of Fort Collins\, CO\, Devens uses her music to explore the vulnerabilities of her own experiences in life and to remind her audience of the importance of self-care. Promoting the message “Take Care of You” both mentally and physically - Devens’ music is for people who can relate to a struggle but still continue to have hope for a brighter day. She shares her story through the intimate lyrics and songs that she creates. Strong\, emotive vocals complement her unique guitar style\, making her a real standout in a sea of singer-songwriters. “If just one person can resonate with my music\, then I will have given back hope like music has given me hope through some of my hardest times.” Britt has released a number of singles and EPs\; her most recent effort\, “Here I Go Again” was released on August 25\, 2023\nEllsworth www.ellsworththefolksinger.com\nMaybe it’s their sincere lyrics or humorous stage presence that makes first time listeners become devoted fans of ELLSWORTH after only two songs. Maybe it’s the way ELLSWORTH presents themselves\, so natural and authentic\, with the fluidity of their gender finding its moment on stage and in their music. Either way\, ELLSWORTH “has a remarkable way of cracking open your soul and finding the hidden corners of your heart you've too long forgotten or didn't even know existed” (Sway Wild\, Dave McGraw and Mandy Fer).With a uniquely powerful voice and a knack for lyrical storytelling\, ELLSWORTH is an artist on the rise in Denver and around the world.Currently\, ELLSWORTH is a finalist in the 2022 Great American Song Contest\, and they recently placed their song\, Growing Pains\, in the Disney+ show Diary of a Future President. “[ELLSWORTH has] a stunningly pure voice\, boundless enthusiasm and a way with words that hugs deep into our hearts. They are a singer-songwriter that is finding their feet and it feels like they will only get better and better through time. Having talent is one thing but being sincere\, putting in the hard work and going for your dreams through undoubted trial and error\, is how you become truly great at what you set your mind to” (AnR Factory\, London\, UK).\nMonica Marie LaBonte monicamariemusic.com\nFrom a wide-eyed tike delicately pressing the keys of her mother’s upright piano to a seasoned artist taking various stages across the country\, Monica Marie LaBonte has always been guided by song.With the sharp ability to craft tracks that speak to the fragility and wonder of life\, the crystalline vocalist continues to attract listeners with her stirring blend of folk and country. At times\, her lyrics come across as wise whisperings from a dear friend. At others\, they hold all the vulnerability and transparency of raw confessions. A keen observer\, LaBonte bears witness to life’s magic and heartache and artfully weaves the intricacies of the human condition into tunes that possess undeniable intimacy\, grace and grit.In her over 10-year career\, the Colorado native has played hundreds of venues\, including the historic Gold Hill Inn and Planet Bluegrass. Whether belting out ballads in a small listening room or playing to tens of thousands at an open-air venue\, she brings a palpable authenticity to each gig.Known for her stint in mystic-Americana band Monocle\, her stellar musicianship and gift for commanding a stage shines just as bright in her solo work.Armed with an acoustic and her truth\, it’s clear LaBonte is pursuing her art for all the right reasons. Although her creative pursuits are guided by pure passion\, LaBonte hasn’t escaped critical praise and success. A finalist In the 2018 Songwriter Showcase\, at Rocky Mountain Folks Fest in Lyons\, Colo.\, she continues to impress with her art.A natural-born wordsmith — in the vein of Joni Mitchell and Alison Krauss — it’s easy to see why the songstress has packed coffeehouses\, held her own on the lineup at the Telluride Bluegrass Festival and been hailed as having “a voice I trust” by fellow musician Daniel Rodriguez (founding member of Elephant Revival).Powerful\, yet understated — poetic\, yet real — LaBonte remains one to watch.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/mixtape-songwriter-showcase-featuring-britt-devens-and-ellsworth
DTEND:20260109T043000Z
LOCATION:The Times Collaborative / 338 Main St
DTSTART:20260109T023000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Folk/Acoustic] MIXTAPE: Songwriter Showcase featuring Britt Devens and Ellsworth
UID:ee1307e6-da75-4f04-b577-30f89a130682@ee13.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:The Delta Sonics music takes a Chicago Blues base and seasons it with Swing\, Delta\, N’awlins R&B and some early Rock n' Roll . This hard -working band averages over 200 shows a year. They have been featured at many of the major festivals in Colorado and have been the back-up band for nationally known Blues artists.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/music-at-bricks-on-main-the-delta-sonics
